**/makerlab/
**/source 3d models/
# Tests are ignored WHOLESALE because five of foldbox's eight reference the unlaunched cut
# half (cutPack / cutFiles / lac), which is fenced out of this repo for the same reason the
# source is. A test that imports fenced code leaks the design just as effectively as the code.
#
# Per-app exceptions below, for apps with nothing fenced to leak. The clicker's suite is the
# only thing proving the fit controls move the geometry they name, and losing it to a blanket
# rule aimed at a different app is the wrong trade.
**/tests/
!apps/clicker-generator/tests/
!apps/clicker-generator/tests/**
!apps/keycap-generator/tests/
!apps/keycap-generator/tests/**
packages/manifold-noeval/README.md

# Paid feature source (anything sold rather than given away). The public
# build never ships these — the branch that mounts them is fenced behind the MAKERLAB
# compile-time flag and resolved through `virtual:pro-pack` — but the SOURCE would still be
# readable in a public repo, which is the whole thing people are paying for.
apps/*/src/pro/

# Unreleased apps. This repo is public and it is the live site, so an app in it is an
# announcement — the whole design, before it is finished and before it is decided whether it
# ships free, paid or at all. It stays on disk and stays a pnpm workspace member, so
# `pnpm --filter laser-slot dev` works exactly as it did; it is simply not published yet.
# Add the app back here and to generators.json (with a build + copy step in deploy.yml, or
# the hub card is a 404) on the day it ships.
#
# It was tracked until 2026-08-17, so it is still readable in the history — removing it
# from HEAD hides it from anyone browsing, not from anyone looking.
apps/laser-slot/

# Laser Toolbox (2026-09-13): the laser editor skeleton — PRD in docs/briefs/laser-toolbox-prd.md.
# Same fence as laser-slot, for the same reason: unreleased, and undecided on free vs paid.
# Its kit half (packages/ui-kit editor-shell.*) IS tracked — it is a component, not the product.
apps/laser-toolbox/

# Laser Keychain (2026-09-17) — the design studio Laser Studio grew out of. Same fence, same
# reason: unreleased. Plan in docs/briefs/laser-keychain-plan.md.
apps/laser-keychain/
#
# SHIPPED 2026-09-22 — apps/laser-studio, packages/laser and packages/patterns came OUT of this
# fence and are tracked. The hub card and deploy.yml build from source, so nothing Laser Studio
# imports can stay fenced: packages/laser (the pure engine — ops, rings, 2D CSG, blanks, keyring,
# text, plus the clicker's tracer) and packages/patterns (the repeating-pattern engine, with the
# 330 Pattern Monster tiles under MIT) are public now. The two unreleased laser APPS — the
# keychain above, the toolbox and laser-slot elsewhere in this file — stay fenced: their engine
# being readable is not the same as their design being on the site. Consequence to live with:
# anything added to those two packages is published the moment it is committed. They are shipped
# code now, not the scratchpad they were until today.
#
# @vostok/elements (the curated CC0 / public-domain vector element library) MOVED OUT of this
# repo entirely on 2026-09-22, to ../vostok-elements — a sibling folder. Nothing in the monorepo
# imports it, Laser Studio never did, and 77 MB of SVG sitting gitignored inside a public repo
# that is also the live site bought nothing. It is not a pnpm workspace member any more; its
# ingest scripts run with plain node from that folder. Only the Library Lab reads it, over the
# relative path in its vite.config.ts.
#
# The Library Lab previews the pattern tiles and that element library and nothing else — still
# unreleased, still fenced.
apps/library-lab/

# @vostok/laser's photo half stays fenced even though the rest of the package shipped (Ian,
# 2026-09-22). It is the AI background-removal feature of the unreleased laser keychain and
# toolbox — `segment.ts` + `segment.worker.ts` and a 4.5 MB `u2netp.onnx` — and Laser Studio
# never imports it: `@vostok/laser/photo` is its own export subpath, `src/index.ts` does not
# touch it, and the built bundle greps clean for `onnxruntime`. Licence was not the question
# (Apache-2.0 model, MIT runtime, both recorded in models/LICENSE-MODELS.md); permanence was.
# A binary in git history cannot be taken back out, and an unlaunched feature in a public repo
# is an announcement — the same rule as the fences above.
#
# Consequence, on purpose: a fresh clone has no `packages/laser/src/photo/`, so the `./photo`
# entry in its package.json resolves to nothing there. Nothing tracked imports it, and the two
# apps that do are fenced too. Un-ignore it on the day that feature launches.
packages/laser/src/photo/

# Foldbox ships PRINT-ONLY (2026-08-26). The app is published; its unlaunched CUT half is
# not. `cutPackPlugin` in apps/foldbox/vite.config.ts already keeps these three modules out
# of the default bundle — this keeps them out of the public tree as well, for the same
# reason as `apps/*/src/pro/` above: a finished-but-unlaunched design is an announcement.
#
# Consequence, on purpose: a fresh clone can run `pnpm --filter foldbox build` (print-only,
# what deploy.yml builds) but NOT `build:full`, `build:offline` or `pnpm --filter foldbox
# dev` — all of which run --mode full and resolve `virtual:cut-pack` to cutPack.ts. Use
# `dev:print` (which is what `pnpm dev:foldbox` runs) in a clone. Un-ignore these on the day
# the cut half launches, together with the phase-2 wording already fenced in index.html.
apps/foldbox/src/export/cutFiles.ts
apps/foldbox/src/export/cutPack.ts
apps/foldbox/src/export/lac.ts
# Cut-half working output and fit rigs — real .svg/.dxf cut files and the scratch harnesses
# that produced them. Same fence, one level out.
apps/foldbox/demo/
apps/foldbox/srcfit/
apps/foldbox/testfit/
apps/foldbox/scripts/
apps/foldbox/offline.README.txt
# The full engineering README, which documents both halves — machine tables, kerf, cut order,
# the glued styles. `apps/foldbox/README.md` is the print-only cut-down of it, and is tracked.
apps/foldbox/README.internal.md

